## single-pack coverer — the earlier claim, at three cadences

  cadence    0: 6/6 rounds   <- the earlier rig
  cadence    6: 0/6 rounds
  cadence 3600: 0/6 rounds   <- SHIPPED

Identical in all three reps. The single-pack form does NOT survive a
real cadence, and "24 of 24" should never have been quoted without it.

## the GREEDY SET — keep a set that holds every reachable object, drop
## a pack when every reachable object it holds is in another KEPT pack

  cadence    0: 105656/105656, 105530/105530, 105657/105657 B
  cadence    6:  86668/86674,   86674/86674,   86673/86673 B
  cadence 3600:  48017/48017,   48017/48017,   48021/48021 B

100% OF THE REDUNDANT BYTES, AT EVERY CADENCE, IN EVERY REP, BUILDING
NOTHING. Greedy collected = drop-and-fsck oracle, exactly.

