## What it means

Direction 4 is FREE — through the SET, not through a single pack. The
reclaim never has to run pack-objects and never has to upload: it reads
reachability once in the quiescent window and writes a shorter pack list.

A second, smaller reading: at the shipped cadence the residue itself is
SMALLER (48,017 B vs 105,656 B at cadence 0) because residue requires a
base rebuild to create it — `--all` is the only thing that drops the
dead objects and so the only thing that leaves an uncoverable input. A
rarer base rebuild makes less residue AND collects it less often.

## Not measured

Wall-clock of the reachability read on a large repository. It is a
rev-list over the refs plus a pass over the pack indices — the same read
fold.rs already does for coverage — but "already does it" is not a
latency measurement, and this window is on the WAKE path.
